Subject: [PATCH] tb710fu: expose security.mac.lockdown_mode_state_public sysctl for macOS 27

macOS 27.3 (26C5035r) launchd calls os_lockdown_mode_enabled() right after
"Early boot complete. Continuing system boot.", which queries
security.mac.lockdown_mode_state_public and aborts (SIGABRT) on ENOENT.
Expose it alongside security.mac.lockdown_mode_state in bsd/kern/lockdown_mode.c.

diff --git a/bsd/kern/lockdown_mode.c b/bsd/kern/lockdown_mode.c
index 1c104b3..e8640c3 100644
--- a/bsd/kern/lockdown_mode.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/lockdown_mode.c
@@ -39,6 +39,7 @@ int lockdown_mode_state = 0;
 
 SYSCTL_DECL(_security_mac);
 SYSCTL_INT(_security_mac, OID_AUTO, lockdown_mode_state, CTLFLAG_RD | CTLFLAG_LOCKED, &lockdown_mode_state, 0, "Lockdown Mode state");
+SYSCTL_INT(_security_mac, OID_AUTO, lockdown_mode_state_public, CTLFLAG_RD | CTLFLAG_LOCKED | CTLFLAG_ANYBODY, &lockdown_mode_state, 0, "Lockdown Mode state (public)");
 
 __startup_func
 void
